<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<meta name="generator" content="Pennsieve neuro-report {{ m.version }}">
<title>{{ m.title }}</title>
<style>
:root {
  --ink: #111827; --muted: #4b5563; --faint: #6b7280; --line: #d9dee5; --soft: #f4f6f8;
  --accent: #1f4e8c; --warn-bg: #fff7e6; --warn-line: #d97706; --warn-ink: #7c2d12;
  --ok: #166534; --ok-bg: #e8f5ec; --bad: #991b1b; --bad-bg: #fdecec;
}
* { box-sizing: border-box; }
html { -webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; }
body { margin: 0; background: #ffffff; color: var(--ink);
  font: 15px/1.55 -apple-system, "Segoe UI", Roboto, "Helvetica Neue", Arial, "DejaVu Sans", sans-serif; }
main { max-width: 980px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 28px 16px 64px; }
h1 { font-size: 27px; line-height: 1.25; margin: 0 0 6px; }
h2 { font-size: 21px; margin: 42px 0 10px; padding-top: 10px; border-top: 2px solid var(--ink); }
h3 { font-size: 16px; margin: 22px 0 6px; }
h4 { font-size: 14px; margin: 16px 0 4px; color: var(--muted); }
p { margin: 6px 0 10px; }
a { color: var(--accent); }
.sub { color: var(--muted); margin: 0 0 4px; }
.meta { display: grid; grid-template-columns: max-content 1fr; gap: 2px 14px; margin: 14px 0; font-size: 14px; }
.meta dt { color: var(--faint); }
.meta dd { margin: 0; }
nav.toc { background: var(--soft); border-radius: 6px; padding: 10px 14px; font-size: 14px; margin: 16px 0; }
nav.toc ol { margin: 4px 0; padding-left: 20px; columns: 2; column-gap: 28px; }
@media (max-width: 640px) { nav.toc ol { columns: 1; } .meta { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
.tablewrap { overflow-x: auto; margin: 8px 0 12px; }
table { border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 13px; width: auto; min-width: 40%; }
th, td { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); padding: 4px 9px; text-align: left; vertical-align: top; }
th { background: var(--soft); font-weight: 600; }
td.num, th.num { text-align: right; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
table.kv th { background: none; color: var(--muted); font-weight: normal; }
.warnbox { background: var(--warn-bg); border-left: 4px solid var(--warn-line); padding: 8px 14px; margin: 12px 0;
  color: var(--warn-ink); border-radius: 0 6px 6px 0; }
.warnbox h3, .warnbox h4 { margin: 4px 0; color: var(--warn-ink); }
.warnbox ul { margin: 4px 0; padding-left: 18px; }
.note { color: var(--muted); font-size: 13px; }
.licbox { background: #eef4fb; border-left: 4px solid var(--accent); padding: 8px 14px; margin: 12px 0;
  border-radius: 0 6px 6px 0; }
.licbox h3, .licbox h4 { margin: 4px 0; }
figure { margin: 18px 0 22px; page-break-inside: avoid; }
figure img { max-width: 100%; height: auto; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 4px; display: block; }
figure img.overview { max-width: min(100%, 720px); border: none; }
figcaption { font-size: 13.5px; color: #1f2937; margin-top: 6px; }
figcaption b { color: var(--ink); }
.badge { display: inline-block; padding: 1px 8px; border-radius: 10px; font-size: 12px; font-weight: 600; }
.badge.ok { background: var(--ok-bg); color: var(--ok); }
.badge.bad { background: var(--bad-bg); color: var(--bad); }
.step-meta { font-size: 13px; color: var(--muted); }
.refs li { margin-bottom: 7px; font-size: 13.5px; }
.refs .unknown { color: var(--bad); }
.params { font-size: 12.5px; }
code { font-family: ui-monospace, "SFMono-Regular", Menlo, "DejaVu Sans Mono", monospace; font-size: 12.5px;
  background: var(--soft); padding: 0 3px; border-radius: 3px; }
details { margin: 8px 0; }
summary { cursor: pointer; color: var(--accent); }
footer { margin-top: 48px; color: var(--faint); font-size: 12.5px; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); padding-top: 10px; }
@media print { main { max-width: none; } h2 { page-break-before: auto; } a { color: inherit; } }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<main>
<header>
<h1>{{ m.title }}</h1>
{% if m.subtitle %}<p class="sub">{{ m.subtitle }}</p>{% endif %}
<dl class="meta">
  <dt>Report written</dt><dd>{{ m.generated }}</dd>
  {% if m.run_window[0] %}<dt>Steps ran</dt><dd>{{ m.run_window[0] }} – {{ m.run_window[1] }}</dd>{% endif %}
  <dt>Steps</dt><dd>{{ m.steps|length }} ({% for s in m.steps %}{{ s.label }}{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %})</dd>
  <dt>Sessions</dt><dd>{{ m.sessions|length }}</dd>
  {% if m.datasets %}<dt>Data</dt><dd>{% for d in m.datasets %}<a href="{{ d.url }}">{{ d.title }}</a>{% if d.dandiset %} (DANDI:{{ d.dandiset }}){% endif %}{% if not loop.last %}; {% endif %}{% endfor %}</dd>{% endif %}
</dl>
</header>

{% if m.licences %}
<section id="licence" class="licbox">
<h3>Usage and licence</h3>
<p>Parts of this analysis come with terms of use. Respect them when you use or share the results.</p>
<ul>{% for l in m.licences %}<li><b><a href="#step-{{ l.index }}">{{ l.step }}</a>:</b> {% for seg in l.segments %}{% if seg.url %}<a href="{{ seg.url }}">{{ seg.text }}</a>{% else %}{{ seg.text }}{% endif %}{% endfor %}{% if l.refs %} Please cite {{ l.refs|refs }}.{% endif %}</li>{% endfor %}</ul>
</section>
{% endif %}

<nav class="toc"><b>Contents</b>
<ol>
  <li><a href="#overview">Overview</a></li>
  {% if m.warnings %}<li><a href="#warnings">Warnings ({{ m.warnings|length }})</a></li>{% endif %}
  {% for s in m.steps %}<li><a href="#step-{{ loop.index }}">{{ s.title }}</a></li>{% endfor %}
  <li><a href="#methods">Methods</a></li>
  <li><a href="#software">Software &amp; provenance</a></li>
  <li><a href="#references">References</a></li>
  <li><a href="#acknowledgements">Acknowledgements</a></li>
  <li><a href="#cite">How to cite this analysis</a></li>
</ol></nav>

<section id="overview">
<h2>Overview</h2>
<p>This report collects the results of {{ m.steps|length }} analysis step{{ 's' if m.steps|length != 1 }} of the
{% for w in m.workflows %}<b>{{ w.name }}</b>{% if not loop.last %}{{ ' and ' if loop.revindex == 2 else ', ' }}{% endif %}{% endfor %} workflow{{ 's' if m.workflows|length != 1 }} on {{ m.sessions|length }} session{{ 's' if m.sessions|length != 1 }}.
Each step's section says what the step does, shows its headline numbers and figures with the captions the step wrote,
and lists its warnings. Numbers and captions are copied from each step's own <code>summary.json</code>; this report
does not recompute them.</p>
{% if overview %}
<figure><img class="overview" src="{{ overview }}" alt="Workflow overview">
<figcaption><b>Workflow overview.</b> The steps of each workflow found in this report, in pipeline order. Filled
boxes are steps whose results are included; grey dashed boxes are steps of the workflow that were not linked into
the report (their results may still exist elsewhere).</figcaption></figure>
{% endif %}
{% if m.sessions %}
<h3>Sessions</h3>
<div class="tablewrap"><table>
<tr><th>Session</th>{% if has_subject %}<th>Subject</th>{% endif %}{% if has_condition %}<th>Condition</th>{% endif %}{% if has_group %}<th>Group</th>{% endif %}<th>Steps with results</th></tr>
{% for r in m.sessions %}<tr><td>{{ r.session_id }}</td>{% if has_subject %}<td>{{ r.subject_id }}</td>{% endif %}{% if has_condition %}<td>{{ r.condition }}</td>{% endif %}{% if has_group %}<td>{{ r.group }}</td>{% endif %}<td>{{ r.steps|join(', ') }}</td></tr>
{% endfor %}</table></div>
{% endif %}
</section>

{% if m.warnings %}
<section id="warnings">
<div class="warnbox">
<h3>Warnings ({{ m.warnings|length }})</h3>
<p>Read these before interpreting the results. Each is repeated in its step's section.</p>
<ul>{% for w in m.warnings %}<li><b>{{ w.step }}:</b> {{ w.text }}</li>{% endfor %}</ul>
</div>
</section>
{% endif %}

{% for s in m.steps %}
<section id="step-{{ loop.index }}">
<h2>{{ loop.index }}. {{ s.title }}</h2>
<p class="step-meta">{{ s.app }} {{ s.version }}{% if s.variant %} · variant {{ s.variant }}{% endif %}{% if s.wall_seconds is not none %} · {{ s.wall_seconds|duration }}{% endif %}{% if s.refs %} · references {{ s.refs|refs }}{% endif %}</p>
{% if s.about %}<p>{{ s.about }}{% if s.run_note %} <b>{{ s.run_note }}</b>{% endif %}</p>{% else %}<p class="note">No description is built into this report for <code>{{ s.app }}</code>; its results are shown as the app wrote them.</p>{% if s.run_note %}<p><b>{{ s.run_note }}</b></p>{% endif %}{% endif %}

{% if s.licence %}<div class="licbox"><h4>Usage and licence</h4><p>{% for seg in s.licence.segments %}{% if seg.url %}<a href="{{ seg.url }}">{{ seg.text }}</a>{% else %}{{ seg.text }}{% endif %}{% endfor %}{% if s.licence.refs %} Please cite {{ s.licence.refs|refs }}.{% endif %}</p></div>{% endif %}

{% if s.warnings %}<div class="warnbox"><h4>Warnings</h4><ul>{% for w in s.warnings %}<li>{{ w }}</li>{% endfor %}</ul></div>{% endif %}

{% if s.overall %}
<div class="tablewrap"><table class="kv">{% for k, v in s.overall %}<tr><th>{{ k }}</th><td>{{ v }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}</table></div>
{% endif %}

{% if s.session_rows %}
<h3>Headline numbers</h3>
{% if s.app == 'nwb-inspect' %}
<div class="tablewrap"><table>
<tr>{% for h in s.session_header %}<th>{{ h }}</th>{% endfor %}</tr>
{% for r in s.session_rows %}<tr>{% for c in r %}{% if s.session_header[loop.index0] == 'DANDI-ready' %}<td><span class="badge {{ 'ok' if c == 'yes' else 'bad' }}">{{ 'DANDI-ready' if c == 'yes' else ('not ready' if c == 'no' else c) }}</span></td>{% else %}<td{% if loop.index0 > 0 %} class="num"{% endif %}>{{ c }}</td>{% endif %}{% endfor %}</tr>{% endfor %}
</table></div>
{% elif s.transpose %}
<div class="tablewrap"><table>
<tr><th></th>{% for r in s.session_rows %}<th class="num">{{ r[0] }}</th>{% endfor %}</tr>
{% for h in s.session_header[1:] %}{% set i = loop.index %}<tr><th>{{ h }}</th>{% for r in s.session_rows %}<td class="num">{{ r[i] }}</td>{% endfor %}</tr>{% endfor %}
</table></div>
{% else %}
<div class="tablewrap"><table>
<tr>{% for h in s.session_header %}<th{% if loop.index0 > 0 %} class="num"{% endif %}>{{ h }}</th>{% endfor %}</tr>
{% for r in s.session_rows %}<tr>{% for c in r %}<td{% if loop.index0 > 0 %} class="num"{% endif %}>{{ c }}</td>{% endfor %}</tr>{% endfor %}
</table></div>
{% endif %}
{% endif %}

{% for t in s.overall_tables %}
<h4>{{ t.name }}{% if t.truncated %} (first {{ t.rows|length }} of {{ t.n_rows }}){% endif %}</h4>
<div class="tablewrap"><table><tr>{% for h in t.header %}<th>{{ h }}</th>{% endfor %}</tr>
{% for r in t.rows %}<tr>{% for c in r %}<td{% if loop.index0 > 0 %} class="num"{% endif %}>{{ c }}</td>{% endfor %}</tr>{% endfor %}</table></div>
{% endfor %}

{% if s.details %}
<details{% if s.n_sessions == 1 %} open{% endif %}><summary>More numbers{% if s.n_sessions > 1 %} for {{ s.details|length }} of {{ s.n_sessions }} sessions{% endif %}</summary>
{% for d in s.details %}
{% if s.n_sessions > 1 %}<h4>{{ d.session }}</h4>{% endif %}
{% if d.lines %}<div class="tablewrap"><table class="kv">{% for k, v in d.lines %}<tr><th>{{ k }}</th><td>{{ v }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}</table></div>{% endif %}
{% for t in d.tables %}
<h4>{{ t.name }}{% if t.truncated %} (first {{ t.rows|length }} of {{ t.n_rows }}){% endif %}</h4>
<div class="tablewrap"><table><tr>{% for h in t.header %}<th>{{ h }}</th>{% endfor %}</tr>
{% for r in t.rows %}<tr>{% for c in r %}<td{% if loop.index0 > 0 %} class="num"{% endif %}>{{ c }}</td>{% endfor %}</tr>{% endfor %}</table></div>
{% endfor %}
{% endfor %}
</details>
{% endif %}

{% if s.figures %}
<h3>Figures</h3>
{% for f in s.figures %}
<figure>{% if f.src %}<img src="{{ f.src }}" alt="{{ f.rel }}">{% else %}<p class="note">(figure could not be read: {{ f.rel }})</p>{% endif %}
<figcaption><b>Figure {{ f.number }}.</b> {{ f.caption or '(no caption in summary.json)' }} <span class="note">({{ f.rel }})</span></figcaption></figure>
{% endfor %}
{% endif %}
{% if s.omitted_figures %}<p class="note">{{ s.omitted_figures|length }} more figure{{ 's' if s.omitted_figures|length != 1 }} of this step (MAX_FIGURES = {{ m.parameters.MAX_FIGURES }}) are in its output folder: {{ s.omitted_figures|join(', ') }}.</p>{% endif %}
{% if s.missing_figures %}<p class="note">Listed in summary.json but missing from the output: {{ s.missing_figures|join(', ') }}.</p>{% endif %}

{% set inl = s.tables|selectattr('inline')|list %}
{% for t in inl %}
<h4>Table: {{ t.rel }}</h4>{% if t.caption %}<p class="note">{{ t.caption }}</p>{% endif %}
<div class="tablewrap"><table><tr>{% for h in t.inline.header %}<th>{{ h }}</th>{% endfor %}</tr>
{% for r in t.inline.rows %}<tr>{% for c in r %}<td>{{ c }}</td>{% endfor %}</tr>{% endfor %}</table></div>
{% endfor %}
{% set rest = s.tables|rejectattr('inline')|list %}
{% if rest %}
<h4>Other tables in the step's output</h4>
<ul class="note">{% for t in rest %}<li><code>{{ t.rel }}</code>{% if t.n_rows is not none %} ({{ t.n_rows|num }} rows){% endif %}{% if t.caption %}: {{ t.caption }}{% endif %}{% if not t.exists %} <b>(missing)</b>{% endif %}</li>{% endfor %}</ul>
{% endif %}

{% if s.parameters %}
<details><summary>Parameters ({{ s.parameters|length }})</summary>
<div class="tablewrap"><table class="kv params">{% for k, v in s.parameters.items() %}<tr><th><code>{{ k }}</code></th><td>{{ v|plain }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}</table></div>
</details>
{% endif %}
</section>
{% endfor %}

<section id="methods">
<h2>Methods</h2>
{% for s in m.steps %}
<p><b>{{ s.title }}.</b> {{ s.methods }}{% if s.main_tools %} ({{ s.main_tools|join(', ') }}){% endif %}{% if s.refs %} {{ s.refs|refs }}{% endif %}.
The step ran as <code>{{ s.app }}</code> {{ s.version }}{% if s.variant %} (variant {{ s.variant }}){% endif %}{% if s.n_sessions %} on {{ s.n_sessions }} session{{ 's' if s.n_sessions != 1 }}{% endif %}; its parameters are listed in <a href="#step-{{ s.index }}">section {{ s.index }}</a>.</p>
{% endfor %}
<p>The report was written by <code>neuro-report</code> {{ m.version }} (Pennsieve), which copies each step's numbers,
figures, captions and warnings from its <code>summary.json</code> and its software versions, parameters and
citations from its <code>provenance.json</code>.</p>
</section>

<section id="software">
<h2>Software &amp; provenance</h2>
<div class="tablewrap"><table>
<tr><th>Step</th><th>Version</th><th>Variant</th><th>Tools</th><th class="num">Run time</th><th class="num">Peak memory</th><th>GPU</th></tr>
{% for s in m.steps %}<tr><td>{{ s.label }}</td><td>{{ s.version }}</td><td>{{ s.variant or '–' }}</td>
<td class="params">{% for k, v in s.tools.items() %}{{ k }} {{ v }}{% if not loop.last %}; {% endif %}{% endfor %}</td>
<td class="num">{{ s.wall_seconds|duration if s.wall_seconds is not none else '–' }}</td>
<td class="num">{{ s.peak_rss_mb|mb }}</td><td>{{ s.gpu or 'none' }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}
</table></div>
<p class="note">Run time and peak memory are what each step recorded in its provenance.json (whole step, all sessions).</p>
</section>

<section id="references">
<h2>References</h2>
<p class="note">The works each step cites in its provenance.json, and the datasets. Author lists, titles and
journals come from the Pennsieve apps' CITATION.cff files, verified against Crossref, DataCite and PubMed.</p>
<ol class="refs">
{% for r in m.references %}<li id="ref-{{ r.n }}">{% if r.known %}{{ r.authors }}. {{ r.title }}. {{ r.where }} <a href="{{ r.url }}">doi:{{ r.doi }}</a>{% elif r.url %}<span class="unknown">DOI only (not in the report's citation table):</span> <a href="{{ r.url }}">doi:{{ r.doi }}</a>{% else %}<span class="unknown">Not a DOI, as the step gave it:</span> {{ r.doi }}{% endif %}</li>
{% endfor %}</ol>
</section>

<section id="acknowledgements">
<h2>Acknowledgements</h2>
<p>These analyses package other people's methods, and the credit for them is theirs. Pennsieve packaged the methods
as platform apps; it did not develop them. The steps in this report are built on:</p>
<ul>
{% for a in m.acknowledgements %}<li><b>{{ a.app }}</b>: {% for sw in a.software %}{% if sw.url %}<a href="{{ sw.url }}">{{ sw.title }}</a>{% else %}{{ sw.title }}{% endif %}{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}</li>
{% endfor %}</ul>
{% if m.datasets %}
<h3>Data</h3>
<ul>
{% for d in m.datasets %}<li>{% if d.creators %}{{ d.creators }}{% if d.year %} ({{ d.year }}){% endif %}. {% endif %}<i>{{ d.title }}</i>{% if d.publisher %}, {{ d.publisher }}{% endif %}{% if d.dandiset %} (DANDI:{{ d.dandiset }}){% endif %}. <a href="{{ d.url }}">doi:{{ d.doi }}</a>{% if d.licence %}, {{ d.licence }}{% endif %} [{{ d.n }}]{% if d.paper %}; described in [{{ d.paper }}]{% endif %}. <span class="note">({{ d.how }}{% if not d.known %}; not in the report's citation table{% endif %})</span></li>
{% endfor %}</ul>
{% endif %}
{% if m.dandisets %}<p>Dandisets named in the session sheet: {% for d in m.dandisets %}<a href="https://dandiarchive.org/dandiset/{{ d }}">DANDI:{{ d }}</a>{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}.</p>{% endif %}
{% if m.dandi %}<p>The data are shared in the Neurodata Without Borders (NWB) format on the DANDI Archive.</p>{% endif %}
</section>

<section id="cite">
<h2>How to cite this analysis</h2>
<p>If you use these results, please cite the methods each step rests on (References {{ m.references|map(attribute='n')|list|refs if m.references else '' }}),
the dataset{{ 's' if m.datasets|length != 1 }} analysed{% if m.datasets %} ({% for d in m.datasets %}doi:{{ d.doi }}{% if not loop.last %}; {% endif %}{% endfor %}){% endif %}, and the Pennsieve apps that ran the analysis, with their versions:
{% for a in m.apps_cited %}{{ a.app }} {{ a.version }}{% if a.repository %} (<a href="{{ a.repository }}">{{ a.repository }}</a>){% endif %}{% if not loop.last %}; {% endif %}{% endfor %}.
Each app's CITATION.cff lists the full references. Keep this report with the results: it records the parameters and
software versions that produced them.</p>
</section>

{% if m.issues %}
<section id="inputs">
<h2>Notes on the inputs</h2>
<p class="note">Places where a step's output does not follow the shared output contract (conventions.md). They do not
change the results above; they are listed for the app maintainers.</p>
<ul class="note">{% for i in m.issues %}<li><b>{{ i.app }}</b> ({{ i.folder }}): {{ i.problem }}</li>{% endfor %}</ul>
</section>
{% endif %}

<footer>Written by Pennsieve neuro-report {{ m.version }} on {{ m.generated }}. A PDF version of this report is
<code>report.pdf</code> next to this file; the same content as data is <code>report.json</code>.</footer>
</main>
</body>
</html>
